{
  "why": [
    "Written register of the runtime (value) surface a plugin author may build on.",
    "It is maintained by hand, not derived from a consumer census: measured on all 78 runtime",
    "exports of the pre-move surface, counting importers misclassified about 20 names in both",
    "directions, because a built-in writes a closed-vocabulary literal instead of importing the",
    "constant that publishes it. A closed vocabulary is published so an author CAN enumerate it, so",
    "the absence of an import disproves nothing.",
    "Type exports are not registered yet. Under preview that gap is named rather than closed; it is",
    "a condition of leaving preview. See docs/plugin-api-compatibility.md.",
    "Changing a list here is the deliberate act that a surface change requires: the law compares",
    "these names against the built declarations and fails on any difference in either direction."
  ],
